Implement user story SKY-004-c: Write vitest + supertest integration tests for all server endpoints

## Story Description
Create src/server.test.ts with at least 8 vitest tests using supertest, covering all endpoint scenarios: /health, /search (valid, missing params, non-numeric adults, default adults), /cheapest (valid, empty→404, missing params), RAPIDAPI_KEY absent→503, client error→500, and / serves HTML from file. SkyscannerClient must be fully mocked so no real HTTP calls occur during test runs.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/server.test.ts contains ≥8 vitest tests covering distinct scenarios: /health (with/without RAPIDAPI_KEY), /search (valid params, missing required param, non-numeric adults, default adults=1), /cheapest (valid, empty→404, missing param), RAPIDAPI_KEY absent→503, SkyscannerClient error→500, GET / serves HTML from file
- SkyscannerClient mocked via vi.mock or equivalent — no real HTTP calls made during `vitest run`
- `npx tsc --noEmit` exits 0 with no type errors
- `vitest run` exits 0 with all tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- Express app exported as 'app' from src/server.ts
- GET /health returns { status: 'ok', uptime: number } with 200 status
- GET / returns { status: 'ok', message: 'Skyscanner app server' } with 200 status
- GET /search and GET /cheapest both use query params: from, to, date, adults
- adults defaults to 1 when not provided - no upper or lower bound validation exists
- validateParams returns { ok: false, error: 'Missing required parameter: from' } for missing from
- validateParams returns { ok: false, error: 'Missing required parameter: to' } for missing to
- validateParams returns { ok: false, error: 'Missing required parameter: date' } for missing date
- validateParams returns { ok: false, error: 'Invalid parameter: adults must be numeric' } for non-numeric adults
- RAPIDAPI_KEY is read from process.env.RAPIDAPI_KEY at module load time, not per-request
- When RAPIDAPI_KEY is falsy, both /search and /cheapest return { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' } with 503 status
- GET /search returns { flights: FlightResult[], count: number, searchedAt: string } with 200 status on success
- GET /cheapest returns a single FlightResult object (not wrapped) with 200 status on success
- GET /cheapest returns { error: 'No flights found' } with 404 status when flights array is empty
- Both routes catch errors and return { error: message } with 500 status - message comes from err.message or 'Unknown error'
- SkyscannerClient constructor takes { apiKey?: string } options bag
- SkyscannerClient.searchFlights takes { origin, destination, date, adults? } and returns Promise<FlightResult[]>
- FlightResult interface has fields: price (number), currency (string), airline (string), departure (string), arrival (string), duration (number), stops (number)
- Server listens on PORT env var or defaults to 3000 only when require.main === module

## Mock Strategy
Use vi.mock('./skyscanner/client') with vi.hoisted(() => ({ SkyscannerClient: vi.fn() })) to mock the constructor, then mockReturnValueOnce with a mock instance containing mock searchFlights method; use vi.stubEnv to set/clear RAPIDAPI_KEY; use beforeEach with vi.clearAllMocks()

## Banned Patterns (must NOT appear in your file)
origin, destination, GET /cheapest returns wrapped object, adults=0 validation, adults upper bound check, RAPIDAPI_KEY checked per-request, @jest/globals, import { jest } from, mock('./client'), mock('../skyscanner/client')

